A1.2: Design the Storage (3 Marks)
SQLite database schema designed with two normalized tables (`stations` and `readings`) to avoid data
redundancy and enable fast indexed queries:
CREATE TABLE stations (
 station_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
 station_name TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL
);
CREATE TABLE readings (
 reading_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
 station_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
 reading_date TEXT NOT NULL, -- ISO format YYYY-MM-DD
 hour INTEGER NOT NULL, -- 0 to 23
 pm25 REAL,
 pm10 REAL,
 no2 REAL,
 temperature REAL, -- Normalized to Celsius
 FOREIGN KEY (station_id) REFERENCES stations(station_id)
);
CREATE INDEX idx_station_date ON readings(station_id, reading_date);
