A2.2: Normalisation (2 Marks)
• Min–Max Normalisation: Formula: X_scaled = (X - X_min) / (X_max - X_min). Scales all PM2.5 readings
strictly between 0.0 and 1.0. Appropriate for visualization scaling and neural network inputs where
bounded ranges are required.
• Z-Score Standardisation: Formula: X_standard = (X - mu) / sigma. Centers data around a mean of 0 with a
standard deviation of 1. Appropriate for statistical anomaly detection and regression models where
outliers need relative weighting.
A2.3: Formatting (1 Mark)
• Standard Date: YYYY-MM-DD (ISO 8601 standard text format).
• Standard Station Names: Standardized Title Case (e.g., 'Adyar', 'Guindy', 'Tambaram') with stripped
whitespaces.
• Standard Numerical Precision: Floating-point numbers rounded to exactly 2 decimal places for pollutants
and temperature.
