Task A5: Design an AI Application for Citizen Complaints (4 Marks)
A5.1: Sentiment and Summary (2 Marks)
• Sentiment Scorer: Lexicon-based scorer maintaining `POSITIVE` and `NEGATIVE` word sets. Scans tokens; if
a negator (`not`, `never`, `no`) appears immediately preceding a sentiment word, its polarity is flipped (+1
becomes -1, and vice versa).
• Extractive Summariser: Extractive summariser that tokenizes text into sentences, scores each sentence
based on the frequency of important keywords, and selects the top-scoring sentence as the summary.
A5.2: Basic Chatbot (2 Marks)
• Rule-Based Chatbot: Rule-based keyword matcher that intercepts queries like 'What is the PM2.5 in Adyar
today?', extracts location and date entities using regex/string parsing, queries the SQLite database, and
formulates a natural language response.
• Limitations: Limited to predefined keyword patterns; cannot handle complex contextual phrasing, typos,
or multi-turn conversational memory.
