B4.2 & B4.3: Production Decision & Indexing
Adding an index on `(station, day)` reduced aggregation query time on 1,000,000+ rows from 0.45 seconds to
0.03 seconds (~15x speedup). For production scale (100+ stations reporting every 15 minutes + 50,000
complaints/month), SQLite with indexed storage handles structured air-quality readings effortlessly, while
lexicon-based sentiment scoring is suitable for fast initial triage, though complex citizen complaints with
sarcasm require fine-tuned transformer models.
